Hello,

Using the S1 sleep state provided by ACPI (echo 1 > 
/proc/acpi/sleep) works well, overall, on my Dell Inspiron 8600 with 
Kernel 2.4.25.

However, I've noticed that the system clock is not updated when the system 
is restored. It simply contains the time at which the system was put into 
the S1 state.

I checked archives (except for this list, the sourceforge archive appears
to be broken) and whatnot for people haveing similar problems and found no
references on the topic of system time restoration.  Is this something
that should be done in user-land, or is it something that will be added to
the kernel in the future?

Please CC: me on any responses, as I am not a member of this list. Thanks,

	-Jeff




